Hi Gary -

The number of tribes in the US has changed to 575, with the addition of one=
 in 2026 according to the Federal Register.  Can you update the web page we=
 are working on to reflect this?

Great to get to know more about the process of video making yesterday - and=
 I appreciate the amazing work you are doing on the new website!

Respectfully,

Jaylene Peterson-Nyren, MBA
Director of Operations
Lutheran Indian Ministries
jpnyren@lutheranindianministries.org

________________________________
From: Robert Heffle <rheffle@lutheranindianministries.org>
Sent: Wednesday, April 8, 2026 7:47 PM
To: Jaylene Peterson-Nyren <jpnyren@lutheranindianministries.org>
Subject: RE: 575 Federally Recognized Tribes in United States


Hi,



Thanks for looking into this, and yes, I would agree that this would be gre=
at information for onboarding new members.



Robert



From: Jaylene Peterson-Nyren <jpnyren@lutheranindianministries.org>
Sent: Wednesday, April 8, 2026 6:34 PM
To: Robert Heffle <rheffle@lutheranindianministries.org>
Subject: 575 Federally Recognized Tribes in United States



Robert -



According to the Federal Register, as noticed by the BIA on January 30, 202=
6, there are a total of 575 Federally Recognized Tribes in the United State=
s.



The link below takes you to the Federal Register where you can also see the=
 full list broken down by the 'lower 48' and Alaska.  This may be a good ar=
ea to cover for Board Training/Onboarding in future as well.



https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/01/30/2026-01899/indian-enti=
ties-recognized-by-and-eligible-to-receive-services-from-the-united-states-=
bureau-of



Jaylene Peterson-Nyren, MBA

Director of Operations

Lutheran Indian Ministries

jpnyren@lutheranindianministries.org<mailto:jpnyren@lutheranindianministrie=
s.org>



